## 4. Canonical role ordering (re-issued as the contract)

1. `measure-strategy` — captures the immutable `phase_base_sha`
   immediately after this strategy commit lands; records that SHA
   in the next strategy artifact. (This step has just landed in the
   lineage; the capture must happen after the strategy commit lands,
   not before — see §6.)
2. `measure-mid-red` (track-local `truth-test-author`) — author the
   freeze contract and admission tests; run Red; route defects to
   Green.
3. `measure-jr-green` (track-local `discovery-auditor` /
   `evidence-collector` / `requirements-mapper`) — implement Green
   for Phase 1 mechanical discovery, Phase 2 human discovery, and
   Phase 3 reconciliation. One canonical subagent is invoked per
   track-local role; the track-local role name is recorded in each
   artifact's `role` / `task_id` / receipt `task_id` field. Frozen
   pairwise isolation, frozen ceilings, and `fork_turns="none"`
   provenance are preserved.
4. `measure-review-a-correctness`, `measure-review-b-security`,
   `measure-review-c-ux-api` in parallel as audit-only roles after
   Jr commits Green work. They write only their supplied audit
   result JSON and route blockers to Green. Their previous outputs
   on disk are stale and remain historical input to the next
   reviewer rerun.
5. `measure-adversarial-testing` (track-local `adversarial-reviewer`)
   — under explicit frozen `adversarial-reviewer` ownership, this
   subagent is the bounded owner of `independent-review.json`,
   `role-receipts/adversarial-reviewer.json`,
   `candidate-denominator-manifest.json`, and
   `candidate-partition-manifest.json`. It is invoked with
   `fork_turns="none"` isolation (or a retained raw export whose
   history starts with exactly the fresh review prompt), measured
   labeled-integer `actual_usage` per frozen ceiling, zero numeric
   stop-loss observations, frozen freshness, ancestor-only inputs,
   prompt/context hashes, output hashes, and no inherited author
   narrative. Defects found are routed to Green via adversarial
   feedback; the affected gates are then rerun. It is invoked once
   after the predecessor admission gate is green and after
   Green-rerouted Review-A/B/C remediation has landed. The
   canonical subagent under this ownership may NOT review its own
   output, drop `fork_turns="none"`, or accept a stale predecessor
   receipt.
6. `measure-phase-acceptance` (audit-only) — invokes only after
   every required Review A/B/C, the `measure-adversarial-testing`
   reviewer rerun, and any UX/browser review (none applicable
   here) target the same final phase HEAD. It writes only its
   supplied audit result.
7. Product-owner exact-hash gate (human, not a canonical subagent)
   — binds the exact candidate/partition/review/predecessor-gate
   hashes in `product-owner-acceptance.json` with a current
   authorization event. This is the non-substitutable authorization
   required to flip candidate manifests from non-consumable to
   accepted.
8. `measure-final-acceptance` (audit-only) — pre-closeout; requires
   every `phase-acceptance` result, the candidate hashes, the
   owner binding, and the global gates (`measure/doctor.sh`,
   `PROJECT_LINT`, `PROJECT_CHECKS`, `PROJECT_TESTS`) to exit 0.
9. `measure-closeout` — moves `measure/tracks/<track>` to
   `measure/archive/<track>`, flips `metadata.json.status` to
   `done`, removes the active track row from `measure/tracks.md`,
   and writes the closeout manifest. Per SKILL §Closeout Standard
   and §Delegation closeout allowance, it is permitted to commit
   within its explicit ownership.

## 5. UX/browser review applicability

`measure-ux-browser-review` is **not applicable** for this track
because the inventory phase tests source evidence and artifact
provenance, not a runnable game route or UX. The strategy records
`UX_REQUIRED=never` for the Phase-4 role gates so that
`measure-orchestrator-audit` and any future re-validation cannot
gate on the absence of a `PROJECT_DEV_URL`. The decision is
re-evaluated only if future evidence changes the determination
(e.g., a downstream successor track publishes a runnable
denominator-aware cartridge); this strategy records the applicable
ground truth, not a permanent bar.

## 6. `phase_base_sha` capture point (orchestrator-owned, not
  strategy-owned)

This correction does not pre-record a `phase_base_sha` because the
capture must happen after this strategy commit is in the lineage,
not before. Per the SKILL §Role Order and the orchestrator's
`strategy_freshness_feedback` predicate in
`measure_interphase_checks.py:243`, the orchestrator must capture
`phase_base_sha` for Phase 4 **immediately after** the strategy
commit lands and must record that SHA in the next strategy
artifact (or in the next Red log if no further strategy update is
needed before the next Mid-Red invocation). The role-base for
this correction is `16f09da8e5b3fa1b74efd60d010bb870d8ec3189`,
which is the immutable previous HEAD; the audit HEAD on this
strategy commit will be the new commit hash. The next-handoff
section below deliberately does not cite a `phase_base_sha` for
this reason — that capture is the orchestrator's responsibility
between strategy and Red.

